                <pb facs="0897" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg773"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix to inclosure in No.
                    152.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Adjutant-General Vincent to Commanding Officer at Fort
                        Brown</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Department of Texas</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >San Antonio, Texas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 29,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to your telegram reporting the death yesterday, at 5 o’clock p.m., of
                    General Servando Canales, commanding a division of the army of Mexico, the
                    major-general by brevet, commanding the department, desires you to convey to the
                    proper military representative his profound sentiments of regret at the decease
                    of so distinguished a soldier, one conspicuous in contributing to the present
                    state of quiet and good feeling along the boundary of the two republics.</p>
                <p>The general directs that you arrange appropriately for assisting at the funeral
                    ceremonies, and on the day thereof that the national flag be placed at
                    half-staff, and a salute of honor, thirteen guns, fired at the moment a given
                    signal shall have indicated the consignment of the body to its resting
                    place.</p>
                <p>Please communicate to these headquarters the date of the funeral, to the end
                    that, as an additional mark of honor and respect, the national flag may, on that
                    day, be ordered at half-staff at all the posts within this command.</p>
                <closer><signed>THOMAS M. VINCENT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Adjutant-General</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
